      correctIndex: 2,
      explanation: `<div style="border-radius:10px; box-shadow:0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; overflow:hidden"><div style="background-color:#01506e; border-radius:8px 8px 0 0; color:white; padding:20px"><h1 style="color:white; margin:0">Comprehensive Income Reporting</h1></div><div style="background-color:white; padding:20px"><div style="background-color:#f9f9f9; border-left:5px solid #0099d4; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Correct Answer</h3><p style="margin:0"><span style="color:#4caf50; font-weight:bold">✓</span> <span style="color:#4caf50; font-weight:bold">Accumulated other comprehensive income is reported in the stockholders&#x27; equity section of the balance sheet.</span></p></div><div style="background-color:#f0f7fa; border-left:5px solid #68d3a7; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Multiple Choice Analysis</h3><p style="margin:0"><span style="color:#f44336; font-weight:bold">✗</span> Choice 1: Comprehensive income must include all changes in stockholders&#x27; equity for the period.</p><p style="margin:0"><span style="color:#f44336; font-weight:bold">✗</span> Choice 2: A separate statement of comprehensive income is required.</p><p style="margin:0"><span style="color:#4caf50; font-weight:bold">✓</span> Choice 3: Accumulated other comprehensive income is reported in the stockholders&#x27; equity section of the balance sheet.</p><p style="margin:0"><span style="color:#f44336; font-weight:bold">✗</span> Choice 4: Comprehensive income is reported in the year-end statements but not in the interim statements.</p></div><div style="background-color:#f9f9f9; border-left:5px solid #0099d4; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Explanation</h3><p style="margin:0">The correct statement is that Accumulated Other Comprehensive Income (AOCI) is reported in the stockholders&#x27; equity section of the balance sheet.</p></div><div style="background-color:#f5f9fc; border-left:5px solid #207bb5; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Why the other statements are incorrect</h3><p style="margin:0">Choice 1: Comprehensive income includes net income plus other comprehensive income, not all changes in stockholders&#x27; equity. Items like dividends and stock issuances affect equity but are not part of comprehensive income.</p><p style="margin:0">Choice 2: A separate statement of comprehensive income is not required. Companies can present comprehensive income in one of several formats, including as part of the income statement or as a separate statement.</p><p style="margin:0">Choice 4: Comprehensive income must be reported in both interim and annual financial statements, not just year-end statements.</p><ul style="margin:0 0 12px 0; padding-left:22px"><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Components of Comprehensive Income</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Comprehensive income consists of</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Net income</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Other comprehensive income (OCI), which includes</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Foreign currency translation adjustments</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Unrealized gains/losses on available-for-sale securities</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Changes in the fair value of qualifying hedges</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Pension and other postretirement benefit adjustments</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Presentation Options for Comprehensive Income</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Companies have three options for reporting comprehensive income</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Single continuous statement - Net income followed by OCI items</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Two separate but consecutive statements - Income statement followed by a statement of comprehensive income</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Statement of changes in equity (no longer permitted for public companies under US GAAP)</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px 0">Example: Accumulated Other Comprehensive Income in Balance Sheet</li></ul><table cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse; margin-top:15px; width:100%"><thead><tr><th style="border-bottom:2px solid #01506e; padding:10px; text-align:left">ABC Company - Stockholders&#x27; Equity Section</th><th style="border-bottom:2px solid #01506e; padding:10px; text-align:left">Amount ($)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Common Stock</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">100,000</td></tr><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Additional Paid-in Capital</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">250,000</td></tr><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Retained Earnings</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">375,000</td></tr><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Accumulated Other Comprehensive Income</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">25,000</td></tr><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Total Stockholders&#x27; Equity</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">750,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="background-color:#eef9f2; border-left:5px solid #68d3a7; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Journal Entry Examples</h3><p style="margin:0">When a company has other comprehensive income items, they will eventually be recorded in AOCI. For example, when there&#x27;s an unrealized gain on available-for-sale securities:</p><p style="margin:0">At the end of the period, OCI items are transferred to AOCI:</p></div><div style="background-color:#01506e; border-radius:0 0 8px 8px; color:white; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:white; margin:0 0 12px 0">Summary</h3><p style="margin:0">Accumulated Other Comprehensive Income (AOCI) is correctly reported in the stockholders&#x27; equity section of the balance sheet. It represents the cumulative balance of other comprehensive income items that have not yet been recognized in the income statement. Companies must report comprehensive income in both interim and annual financial statements, and have options for how to present it, but a separate statement is not strictly required.</p></div></div></div>`,
